  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Inclusive Resilience in Somalia (IRiS)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Somalia):  With FY 2024 funds, USAID will promote livelihood and income diversification, increase social and economic connections, facilitate access to finance in rural and urban areas at the community and at the broader systemic level, by influencing policies that impact the community as a whole. For communities involved in the livestock sector, USAID will support a private sector to adopt drought-tolerant fodder varieties. USAID will expand rural, climate-smart investment opportunities and strengthen associations and cooperatives in priority sectors..To advance livelihood diversification and adaptation, USAID will target the fisheries sector in several coastal communities. To build social and economic connections and access to finance for marginalized communities, USAID will increase the capacity and accessibility of economic associations, such as fisheries cooperatives, Village Savings and Loans Associations, self-help groups, and agricultural industry associations. In addition, IRiS will focus on enhancing the Somali Seafood Export Association, a platform connecting export market actors. This will involve providing strategic technical assistance, developing governance structures, and expanding the association&apos;s membership base. IRiS aligns to Gender Equity and Equality Action Fund Priorities 3 and 5. Under priority 3, IRiS will support women&apos;s economic future by helping smallholder women farmers build resilience to climate change by adopting climate-smart livelihoods. Under priority 5, IRiS will expand women&apos;s access to political and social opportunities and strengthen their active decision-making capacity. Through its Gender Inclusion and Disability Action Plan, IRiS promotes equal access to all economic opportunities.. Availability of nutritious foods, will indirectly improve nutrition. .IRiS attributes $1,500,000 to Adaptation-Indirect and will promote livelihood and income diversification towards more resilient and climate-smart livelihoods. ...</narrative>
  </description>
